  "entry": "code/demo/app.py",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Lets a toxicologist go through 405 ToxCast/Tox21 endpoints and see where a Cell Painting morphology model has a certified advantage over a cell-count-only baseline after correcting for multiple tests. It also covers calibration, per-compound predictions, enrichment by assay family, example images and sample-size planning for an organ-on-chip study. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
